# OpenBSD source set — NOT hash-locked by design: fetch-distfiles.sh is
# version-agnostic and resolves the newest published stable release at fetch
# time (probes $ver/amd64/SHA256 on cdn.openbsd.org; override with
# ABZU_OPENBSD_VER=x.y to pin). A static src.tar.gz hash would break every
# release cycle, so integrity comes from the co-fetched signed SHA256
# manifest (openbsd-sha256.txt), verified downstream by the userland import.
# Historical note: the 7.6 tree vanished from primary mirrors (404) and the
# old "TBD" pin was never resolvable there; superseded by auto-resolution
# 2026-10-10. Do not re-add lock entries for these two filenames.
